# What the build context does not need.
#
# Without this the context is roughly 800 MB before a single layer is built:
# `frontend/node_modules` (210 MB), the downloaded weights under `models`
# (155 MB) and the local `storage` tree (434 MB, including the developer's own
# SQLite database and every result they have produced). None of it belongs in
# an image, and the storage tree in particular should never leave the machine.
#
# `docker/Dockerfile.backend` needs three things from above `backend/`:
# `models/manifest.json`, `scripts/download_models.py` and `backend/` itself.
# The rules below keep those and exclude their neighbours.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ heavy
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
storage/

# The weights are fetched during the build, verified against the manifest.
# Copying a developer's local checkpoints in would skip that check and add
# 155 MB, including models this image deliberately does not carry.
models/*
!models/manifest.json

# --------------------------------------------------------------- research
# Benchmarks, their measurements and their crops are not part of the service.
backend/benchmarks/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ python
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*.egg-info/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- local
.git/
.github/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.DS_Store
*.log

# ------------------------------------------------------- not built here
# The frontend is deployed separately on Vercel.
frontend/
docs/
docker/
scripts/*
!scripts/download_models.py
